# Privacy and compliance (overview v3.1)

Privacy is **by default**. Profile owners control what is public. Comply with **Qatar / GCC** data-protection requirements (collection, purpose, retention, access, deletion).

## Contact visibility

- Email and phone are each **independently** public or private
- Private phone: hide entirely **or** show **Request phone** — never leak the number in HTML, QR payloads, or API preview responses
- Public fields may appear on the business card; private fields must not

```ts
// ❌ BAD — send phone on public preview because the owner has one
return { phone: profile.phone }

// ✅ GOOD — honor visibility on every surface (web preview, app card, QR)
return { phone: profile.phonePublic ? profile.phone : { status: 'private' } }
```

## Product surfaces

- Rater identity when they rate someone: **title shown, name kept private** (same choice for every rater)
- Do not log or cache private contacts in analytics, crash reports, or email signatures beyond what the owner marked public
